      "topic_id": "congruent_triangle_proof_foundation",
      "prompt": "M is the midpoint of AB. P is a point such that PM is perpendicular to AB. Which congruence criterion proves that the two triangles are congruent? A) SSS  B) SAS  C) ASA  D) RHS",
      "solution_steps": [
        "AM = BM (M is the midpoint of AB)",
        "angle AMP = angle BMP = 90° (PM is perpendicular to AB)",
        "PM is common to both triangles",
        "These facts match the Side-Angle-Side (SAS) congruence criterion."
      ],
      "final_answer": "B) SAS",
      "marks": 1,
